1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,590
Good morning, North College Library. How can I help you?

2
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:06,740
I was wondering if it was possible to join the library.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:09,000
Are you a student at North College?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,220
No, I'm not, but someone told me it was possible to join, even if I wasn't.

5
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:18,150
That's right, it is. Are you over 18? That's our minimum joining age.

6
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:21,000
Yes, I am. That's no problem then.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,900
Could you tell me what I have to do to join?

8
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:28,667
Well, you'll need to come in to the library and fill out some forms.

9
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:32,073
You'll also need to bring two passport photos with you.

10
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:36,840
We also need two documents for ID, so a driving licence would be fine.

11
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:40,920
I've got that and what else? A credit card?

12
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,900
No, it needs to have your address on it.

13
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:47,820
Shall I bring a bank statement, would that do? That'll be fine.

14
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:51,190
Good. Does it cost anything to join?

15
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:53,732
Well, it's free for students here

16
00:00:53,732 --> 00:00:58,100
but otherwise it's £125 per year or £25

17
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:01,360
if you've got a current student card from another college.

18
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:04,500
I was at Westerley College until last year

19
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,998
but now I've got a job at Jefferson's steel factory.

20
00:01:08,998 --> 00:01:14,090
Er, it's more expensive than I thought. My local library is free.

21
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:17,800
But you'll find they don't have the range of reference books or facilities

22
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,562
which we buy for our students.

23
00:01:19,562 --> 00:01:22,730
That's why you have to pay to be an external member.

24
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:26,740
I see. How many books can I borrow?

25
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:30,960
We allow twelve items borrowed at any one time if you're a student

26
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,133
and that includes CDs, DVDs and videos.

27
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:37,830
However, it's only eight items for members of the public.

28
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:41,160
Fine. And how long can I have them for?

29
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:44,160
Well, you can have both fiction

30
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:47,800
and reference books for four weeks which isn't bad really.

31
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:50,100
And what happens if I return them late?

32
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,410
Like all libraries there's a fine system in place.

33
00:01:53,410 --> 00:02:00,270
The minimum fine is 1.50 but it can be much higher for some items-up to 5 per week.

34
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:03,540
We'll give you a booklet with all the details when you join.

35
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:08,260
You can always renew items if they're not required by anyone else

36
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:12,500
by telephoning or logging on to our website.

37
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,170
What about the computers? Can I use them free of charge?

38
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:20,130
For college students it's free, but for external members like yourself,

39
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:26,250
the first hour is free and then we make a nominal charge of £1 per hour thereafter.

40
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:28,850
Do I have to book in advance for them?

41
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:33,265
Oh, yes, it's advisable. Most people tend to book twenty-four hours in advance

42
00:02:33,265 --> 00:02:37,000
although sometimes you can get one with only six hours' notice.

43
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,842
However, the earliest you can book a computer is forty-eight hours before you need it,

44
00:02:41,842 --> 00:02:45,070
and you can only book one hour at a time.

45
00:02:45,070 --> 00:02:47,880
If no-one else has booked the computer out

46
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:51,158
then you may be able to have another hour if you want.

47
00:02:51,158 --> 00:02:55,420
We have a wide range of databases, so the computers are in great demand.

48
00:02:55,420 --> 00:03:01,740
I'm thinking of doing some writing and I might need to access national newspapers.

49
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,900
Do you have them on these databases?

50
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,820
We do indeed. We've got all the big nationals

51
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:10,683
The Guardian and The Observer, The Independent

52
00:03:10,683 --> 00:03:12,660
and The Times and Sunday Times

53
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:17,550
We've also got all the local papers and a wide selection of magazines.

54
00:03:17,550 --> 00:03:21,780
Excellent. I assume you have photocopying facilities?

55
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:26,940
Of course. 5p a sheet for both A4 and A3 black, and-white copies

56
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,590
and 40p a sheet for colour.

57
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:33,130
You can get a card from the counter here. It doesn't take coins.

58
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:38,735
OK. Oh by the way, another thing I was wondering about was

59
00:03:38,755 --> 00:03:42,050
if you ran any writing classes through the library

60
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:46,686
We do, but you'll have to speak to John Grantingham about that.

61
00:03:46,686 --> 00:03:50,550
He's our resident author. He runs the creative writing classes.

62
00:03:50,550 --> 00:03:54,790
John... Grant... Could you spell that for me please?

63
00:03:54,790 --> 00:04:03,910
Certainly. G - R - A - N - T - I - N - G - H - A - M.

64
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,770
Are the classes here at the library?

65
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:12,608
Yes. He's here on Thursday evenings, oh no sorry, Friday. He's just changed it.

66
00:04:12,608 --> 00:04:16,500
You can contact him by emailing the library.

67
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:21,141
Okay. Right, well that's about all I need to know.

68
00:04:21,141 --> 00:04:26,710
Thank you. I'll be along later this week to join. Thanks. Bye.
